  nonce: ba1f  # ba1f
  message: "Web search result: both blocking bugs still unresolved, and the pattern is broader than originally documented.\n\nBUG 1 — PostToolUse additional_context dropped. Still present. Active forum threads (2-3 weeks old as of Apr 2026):\n- https://forum.cursor.com/t/cursor-hooks-additional-context-not-injected-in-agent-context-in-posttooluse/156157\n- https://forum.cursor.com/t/native-posttooluse-hooks-accept-and-log-additional-context-successfully-but-the-injected-context-is-not-surfaced-to-the-model/155689\nHook runs, returns valid JSON with additional_context, log shows accepted — model never sees it. Same symptom on MCP tool calls per anthropics/claude-code#24788, suggesting a shared upstream rendering path rather than a Cursor-only parser bug.\n\nBUG 2 — AfterAgentResponse agent_message/user_message regression. Still present across multiple versions:\n- https://forum.cursor.com/t/regression-hook-response-fields-usermessage-agentmessage-ignored-in-v2-0-64/141516 (original v2.0.64)\n- https://forum.cursor.com/t/regression-hook-response-fields-user-message-agent-message-still-ignored-in-windows-v2-0-77/142589 (still broken in v2.0.77)\n- https://forum.cursor.com/t/hooks-still-not-working-properly-in-2-1-6/143417 (still broken in v2.1.6)\n- https://forum.cursor.com/t/when-are-you-going-to-fix-hooks/148573 (meta thread)\nRegression has survived v2.0.64 -> v2.0.77 -> v2.1.6+ untouched. No indication of an upcoming fix in the Cursor changelog.\n\nRELATED FAILURE MODES (not in the original WI description, widen blast radius):\n- sessionStart hook has the same accept-then-drop symptom: https://forum.cursor.com/t/sessionstart-hook-output-is-accepted-and-merged-but-the-injected-context-does-not-reach-agent-window/157141\n- afterAgentResponse and afterAgentThought don't fire at all in the headless CLI: https://forum.cursor.com/t/hooks-afteragentresponse-afteragentthought-not-firing-in-headless-cli/156220\n- Stop hook runs in the wrong working directory: https://forum.cursor.com/t/stop-hook-uses-wrong-or-different-working-directory-when-executing/157195\n\nPattern: systemic issue in Cursor hook-output processing, not three independent defects. A Cursor-internal refactor around 2.0.64 probably ripped out the bidirectional-hook plumbing and the replacement is still incomplete in 2.1.6+.\n\nRECOMMENDATION: leave WI-rijoj-rukov blocked and todo_soft. SQLite-extractor plumbing still makes no sense to build while injected context can't reach the model on ANY Cursor hook point — not just the two originally named. Revisit when Cursor changelog mentions a hook-output fix, or when a forum thread confirms context flowing again. Cursor is already enforced single-session-per-repo via cursor/session-start.sh sibling check, so immediate risk is covered."  # ba1f
